{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the exact-path succession recut at d1dd3d01c0720af718509e11bf9f8b054a45adbc (request/specific-path-succession-current, one commit on main c3169d83; exactly the seven cited paths, +81/-69; Rests-On governing request e758e940; artifacts rest on promise b4f5e4db; nothing stale or retired). Review against request 15105; not merged.\n\nWhat holds. The central new behaviour is real and mutation-proved on a detached checkout: planSuccession's landed branch publishes at the literal changed path and retires only live artifacts whose Path string equals it (routing publication to a covering directory fails TestMergePublishesTheChangedPathInsteadOfACoveringDirectory at succession_test.go:153; prefix matching fails it at :157; skipping the exact-path retirement fails TestMergeClassifiesEveryCoveredLiveArtifact at :90; dropping the leftLive seal fails it at :98); the cross-author reviewed-path refusal as a pure function fails TestMergePreflightRefusesACrossAuthorRetirementOutsideTheApprovedTree at :248 when disabled; the dot and comma path refusal fails TestMergePreflightRefusesInvalidGeneratedArtifactPaths; deleted and renamed sources retire with no successor at the old path (tests at :197 and :184); the successor-not-published refusal fails main_test.go:1633. Gates at the head: gofmt, go build, go vet, git diff --check clean; go test ./... -count=1 all 34 packages ok including cmd/gs (324.8s), internal/docset, internal/app and internal/workroom. The fold is untouched. Wider covering artifacts are no longer retired by a modification, which is the narrowing the request asked for.\n\nFive changes before approval.\n\n1. The reviewed-path guard's call site lost its only red proof. cmd/gs/main.go:644-651 says the guard runs in fresh preflight before HEAD moves and before any durable record is appended. At base c3169d83, deleting that call fails TestMergeFreshPreflightRefusesACrossAuthorPointerAboveTheReviewedPath (main_test.go:1938, \"error = nil, want a refusal\"). At this head the same deletion leaves ./cmd/gs green, because the head rewrote that test into a success case; the guard survives only as a pure function. Nothing now proves mergeCommand calls it, or that the refusal precedes the HEAD move and cleans the receipt reservation. Add an end-to-end case that reaches the guard through mergeCommand and asserts HEAD, depth and the reservation are unchanged.\n\n2. That test's name and comment now assert the opposite of its body: main_test.go:1921-1925 says the merge \"is refused in preflight\" and :1926 is still named Refuses, while :1934-1936 asserts err == nil and that HEAD moved. Rename it and rewrite the comment, or restore the refusal case as a separate test.\n\n3. The left-live accounting the head documents is false. A live artifact at a strictly wider covering path is classified by successionPredecessors but discarded by landed, so it is neither retired nor sealed: with a live artifact at a parent directory and a change to a file under it, the plan's leftLive is empty. Four sentences in the head's own text say otherwise: AGENTS.md:76 \"Keep other live candidates live, but seal each one in the receipt\"; SKILL.md:232 \"classifying every other live candidate that covers the change\"; SKILL.md:263 \"Account for every other covering candidate in the paired receipt fields\"; docs/reference/architecture.md:844 \"The receipt also accounts for every other live artifact covered by the first-parent diff\", nine lines below the new paragraph at :829. The fold's missingLeftLiveAtReceipt (internal/workroom/fold.go:1616) then files those entries under an empty closest-covering path, producing no receipt debt and no SuccessionUnrecorded, so the abandoned-candidate cleanup prompt SKILL.md:268 calls durable is silently lost. Either seal wider covering candidates in leftLive or make the four sentences and the fold's expectation say what the plan does.\n\n4. Rename contradicts the head's own rules. A rename inside a covered directory retires and republishes the covering pointer (probe: R cmd/gs/a.go to cmd/gs/b.go with a live artifact at cmd/gs publishes cmd/gs and cmd/gs/b.go and retires cmd/gs), because the removed branch (succession.go:191-207) keeps the widest-covering republication for rename sources. AGENTS.md:74-76 says a wider covering pointer \"stays live, and is not selected for retirement by this plan\" for a renamed destination, and docs/reference/gs/merge.md:256 says \"a wider covering pointer stays live\" on rename. Align code and text.\n\n5. The deletion path has no red proof. The governing request named it (\"a removed file may republish the widest covering directory\") and asked for mutation-sensitive delete and rename cases. Deleting the whole widest-covering block in removed (succession.go:199-207) leaves ./cmd/gs green, while SKILL.md:271, architecture.md:833-835 and merge.md:257 all assert the behaviour. Add the test.\n\nRecorded, not blocking: directory-path artifacts become unretireable by merge (five live artifacts at cmd/gs cover three of this head's own files and no merge will ever change a file literally named cmd/gs; they need hand supersession by their authors or a ratifier, and no doc says so); log growth is now one artifact per changed file (main_test.go:1012 moved from 2 to 181 publishes for a 181-file merge) and neither architecture.md nor merge.md records it; a tracked path containing a comma is now unmergeable because every changed file is a publish path and preflightSuccession rejects commas (latent, none tracked today); docs/reference/gs/publish.md:19-20 \"retires the predecessors that cover them\" is now false and is outside the artifact set.\n\nArchitecture: layers five (internal/workroom contract text) and seven (cmd/gs merge adapter). The head publishes docs/reference/architecture.md with the new paragraph at :829, but leaves :844 contradicting it (item 3) and AGENTS.md and merge.md contradicting the rename behaviour (item 4), so the contract page is not internally consistent at this head. The fold contract is unchanged.\n\nSecurity: the authority boundary is narrowed, not widened: modifications no longer reach above the changed path. Deletions and rename sources still reach the widest covering directory and refuseUnreachableCrossAuthorRetirements still bounds that for other actors' artifacts as a function; path handling is byte-exact, non-UTF-8 paths are rejected, -z diffs are unquoted. The defect is item 1: the guard's call site lost the proof that it runs before HEAD moves, a regression against base.\n\nSimplification: landed and removed call covering(path, true), which walks every live artifact building prefix matches, then keep only the exact-path entry; scanning live directly is shorter and makes covering's includeExact parameter dead. widest's fallback parameter is unreachable (its only caller guards len(covers) == 0); the comment at succession.go:153-157 explains a call site that no longer exists; assign's widerPath tie-break is dead; successionPredecessors, coveredArtifacts and protectionIndex still compute provenance closure for wider covering artifacts that assign now discards.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2c9a88e03586f449f94c8d70c6ac7883c2218c69","head":"d1dd3d01c0720af718509e11bf9f8b054a45adbc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:70bb4d4dae794e1811f25838f08c658ff2825d90\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4199156471f5827fa84f62f7f390c2e7bcbba4d0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}